# ── INSTALLERS ARE RELEASE ASSETS, NOT REPOSITORY CONTENT ────────────────────
#
# This is the only rule here that does any work, and it is a guard rather than housekeeping.
#
# A repository that accumulates binaries grows without bound and never shrinks: git keeps every
# version of every object forever, so `git clone` becomes a download of every installer ever
# shipped, and `git filter-repo` plus a force-push is the only way back. It is much easier to
# prevent than to undo.
#
# The README says "no installers in git". These lines are what makes that true rather than a
# request — an installer dropped in this directory while testing a release cannot be committed by
# accident.
*.dmg
*.exe
*.zip
*.blockmap
SHA256SUMS.txt
sbom-*.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
